---
description: Nosy — the nosy product manager that lives inside your coding agent. Apply for product-decision requests like "what can we build next", "can we do this", "what shipped this week", "what's ready in the backend", "what did rivals do", "roadmap", "write a PRD". Do NOT use for code review (bugs, style, quality).
alwaysApply: false
---

Full instructions, command list and rules for Nosy live in the root `AGENTS.md` — this file doesn't repeat them, it points to them. Step-by-step command instructions: `skill/commands/<move-in|tour|peek|psst|canwe|atlas|neighbors|overheard|spill|scoop|roadmap|tea|stakeout>.md`.

If the user asks for any Nosy command (`move-in`, `tour`, `map`, `doctor`, `shipped`, `peek`, `overheard`, `psst`, `frontyard`, `dresscode`, `neighbors`, `canwe <question>`, `atlas`, `spill <topic>`, `scoop`, `roadmap`, `handoff`, `tea`, `stakeout`, `bet`, `score`) (by exact command name or with an equivalent request like "what can we build"):

1. Read `AGENTS.md` first (the command table and general rules are there).
2. Read the matching `skill/commands/<name>.md` file and follow its steps from start to finish.
3. Follow `skill/rules.md`: the decision belongs to the owner, every claim has a source, nothing is written externally (push/PR/issue/message) without the owner explicitly asking, the result goes to a durable file/page under `pm/`.

Cursor has no Claude Code-specific Artifact/AskUserQuestion/sub-agent concepts; in that case use the equivalents from the "Generalizing the agent-specific steps" section of `AGENTS.md` (a file under `pm/` instead of a published page, a plain-text question instead of a structured one, working in your own session in sequence instead of a sub-agent).
